# CLAUDE.md is a GENERAT of the seven fragments in rulebook/ — they carry the same deploy
# host and IP the monolith did, so they are ignored for exactly the same reason it is.
rulebook/
# graphify (code knowledge graph) — machine-local artifacts, never tracked (public repo + lanes must stay clean)
graphify-out/
# graphify hook config carries a machine-local absolute path (account name) — advisory hook stays local-only
.claude/settings.json
inspektion-register.jsonl

# uploads the owner drops into a session (POST /api/slots/:id/upload). Ignored on purpose: an
# untracked file blocks a lane land, and the route REFUSES to write where this line is missing.
# Keeping a drop is then a deliberate `git add -f` — losing it is the default.
drops/

# backups of the deploy identity. `.env` above is ignored, its copies were not: a `.env.bak-<ts>`
# sat untracked in this PUBLIC repo carrying the real host, IP and share URLs (measured 2026-08-22).
# One `git add -A` would have published them.
.env.bak*
